sented on a  theater screen instead of first person  and actions like climbing ladders or  jumping through windows are in third  person  the vr version of resident evil 4 was  revealed back in april but if vr isn't  quite your thing then a remake of the  game was rumored to be in the works  right now while its release date is  still nowhere to be seen blizzard is  finally starting to reveal some of the  character reworks and other details that  you can expect for overwatch too brand  new gameplay was revealed showcasing the  changes to sombra and bastion sombra the  game's hacking fiend potentially has the  more contentious changes among the duo  overall she'll be able to go on the  assault more often thanks to some  serious buffs to her hack ability which  now refreshes every 3 seconds enemies  who are hacked still can't use their  abilities although that's just for a  single second after being hacked for the  duration of the hack though which lasts  8 seconds targets are highlighted and  can be seen through walls hack targets  also take a whopping 50  more damage from sombra giving the  character a mean one-two punch of  hacking a target then peppering them  with bullets similarly sombra's ultimate  has been changed while it no longer  disables shields it deals damage to any  enemies in its radius for a total of 40  off their current health naturally any  enemy caught in the blast is also hacked  so sombra can easily take down enemies  she hits sombra's changes are a series  of buffs and nerfs but bastion has  largely been reworked some changes are  obvious after first looking at its ui  which is now missing a button for  self-repair instead bastion's alt-fire  ability sends out an explosive orb that  can bounce off of surfaces and stick to  players making it perfect for spamming  into choke points for area denial the  robot's regular gun has also changed  firing at a lower rate but losing all of  its spread making it kind of a dmr for  players to pick at enemies 